  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Malaria - Angola (01-Jul-2016-30-Jun-2018)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Angola, Malaria, World Vision International (WV - HQ)This program has the following goals: Accelerated reduction of maternal, infant and under-five mortality.  Reduce by 60% the morbidity and mortality of malaria in the country by 2020 compared to baseline in 2014. The objectives of this program are: By 2020, strengthen the epidemiology surveillance system, monitoring and evaluation and operational research.  By the end of 2020, 100% of malaria cases testing positive are treated according to the national guidelines, at all levels of the national health pyramid, including at community level.  By the end of 2020, 100% of suspected malaria cases at health facility, private pharmacies and community levels are tested before receiving treatment.  By the end of 2020, at least 80% of the target population uses an adequate preventive measure.  Operationalize the health care delivery services at community level and at each of the three levels of the health pyramid by meeting the expectations of the population</narrative>
  </description>
